\item We introduce Twin-DAgger, an explore-correct-augment framework that amplifies each human intervention into a diverse set of targeted digital twin demonstrations, reducing human annotation cost while improving policy robustness.
\item We design a dual-axis augmentation strategy that concentrates synthetic data generation around failure-prone spatial regions and critical temporal windows identified from expert corrections, ensuring each intervention produces training samples where the policy needs them most. 
\item Through experiments on real-world manipulation tasks, including pick and place \boxin{pick-and-place?} and complex peg insertion, we demonstrate that Twin-DAgger outperforms both standard digital twin methods and conventional real-world DAgger baselines using only 10\% of the human intervention budget. 
